(* ============================================================================
   PART 8: PARSING PRECEDENCE
   ============================================================================ *)

(*
   Block parsing precedence (first pass):
   1. Frontmatter (--- delimited at document start)
   2. Comments (%% line, %%% block)
   3. Raw blocks (```=FORMAT -- matched before ordinary fences),
      then code blocks (``` or ~~~ fenced)
   4. Headings (# prefix)
   5. Thematic breaks (---, ***, ___)
   6. Block quotes (> prefix)
   7. Definitions (link/footnote/abbreviation definition lines) and
      block-attribute lines ({...} alone on a line, PART 9 §15)
   8. Lists (-, * bullets at any indent; ordered markers; :: definition
      lists)
   9. Tables (| prefix)
   10. Colon fences (::: -- admonition with type word, line block with |,
       local hard-break block with \, generic div when bare; longest-token
       wins: a `::: x` line is never a `:: ` definition term)
   11. Paragraphs (everything else)
   Recognition order is NOT interruption: which of these may interrupt an
   open paragraph is PART 9 §10.

   Inline parsing (second pass) is PART 9 §9: pass P1 takes atoms in
   the order of its atom table (escapes, code spans, math, inline
   literals, autolinks and cross-references, comments, inline notes, note
   references, bracket runs and their tails), and pass P2 pairs bare,
   braced, combined and editorial spans in one left-to-right reading.
   Prefer literal text over markup: a delimiter that pairs with nothing
   under §9 is literal. What remains is read afterwards, in this order:
   1. Extensions (:type[content])
   2. Mentions and tags (@user, #tag)
   3. Smart typography (--, ---, etc.; `=>` is the arrow, never a
      highlight opener, PART 9 §8)
   4. Trailing line comments (%%, PART 9 §21)
   5. Plain text
*)

